1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
This 600-year-old wall took 350 million bricks — each one signed.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,300
I'm your China Travel Expert.

3
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:06,900
It's not the Great Wall — it wraps the city of Nanjing.

4
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,300
At 35 km, it's the longest city wall on Earth.

5
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:11,900
Ming workers stamped every brick with its maker's name.

6
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,500
If a section failed, they knew exactly who to blame.

7
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,900
Double-tap if you'd trust your name on a brick.

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:19,300
200,000 people built it in about 20 years.

9
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,900
Around 21 km still stands, up to 12 meters high.

10
00:00:21,900 --> 00:00:25,500
★ Expert Tip: Walk Zhonghua Gate — its hidden chambers once hid 3,000 soldiers.

11
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:28,400
Great Wall or Nanjing's wall — which would you walk?
